  Well, maybe I'm just a wimp, but 3.0 is really frustrating.  It's
just too deadly on the first levels.  Orcs on level 1!  Jackalweres
on level 2!  Killer bees on level 3!  Unless there are some new
spoilers I haven't heard of yet, I don't see how a character can
survive long enough for the game to get interesting.  There are
dozens of new bad things that can happen to you, and the monsters
all seem to hit harder, and the old tricks that made 2.3 playable
seem to have been taken away.  (All but Elbereth, and even that
has been weakened.)  Have you designers actually tried to PLAY
the game you designed?

  Examples:
  1)  I managed to get down to level 3 (I'm a wizard with a ring of
regeneration; without that ring a wizard isn't worth bothering with).
All of a sudden four killer bees materialized around me.  With my
wand of sleep I managed to paralyze all of them, and my kitten and
I killed off three, but that fourth bee was invincible.  Bees don't hit
as hard as they used to, and with the help of my wand of sleep and
my ring of regeneration, my kitten and I were able to take over a 
hundred shots at the bee, but neither of us hit it one single time!
Eventually it killed me when I fainted from hunger.

  2)  In my best game so far, I had the extraordinary luck to be a
wizard with a ring of regeneration and two good wands (magic missile
and lightning).  I made it down to level 5, and ran into an Opulent
Throne Room.  Well, I stood in the doorway and let the creatures crowd
in front of me and zapped them with the wand of lightning -- four zaps
was enough to almost clear out the room.  All that was left was one
lousy orc; I figured with 12 hit points left and an armor class of 0
I could afford to take on the orc hand-to-hand and preserve my wand.
But the orc took one swing with his sword and I was dead.

  These are only the most dramatic and irritating ways I've died --
usually I just get chewed up on level 1 or level 2.  The deepest I've
been was level 9, and that was by getting level-teleported from level
4.  Searching frantically for an up-staircase, I promptly ran into
a pack of wolves and got annihilated.

  Don't get me wrong, I think all the new ideas are fantastic -- it's
just that the player needs to have a little bit better chance of 
surviving.


